   ERRATA NOTICE REGARDING TOLK SERVICE LIFE EXTENSION DATES IN
                   COMPREHENSIVE STIPULATION

       Southwestern Public Service Company (“SPS”), New Mexico Department of Justice, New

Mexico Large Customer Group, Occidental Permian Ltd., Louisiana Energy Services LLC,

Federal Executive Agencies, Targa Resources Corp., Walmart Inc., Coalition for Clean Affordable

Energy, and Prosperity Works (collectively, the “Signatories”) submit this Errata Notice to correct

a typographical error in the Comprehensive Stipulation, filed in this proceeding on June 22, 2026

(the “Stipulation”).

       On page 5 of the Stipulation, paragraph 1.2(i), the Signatories agree to SPS’s proposal to

extend the service lives of Tolk Units 1 and 2, and to adjust the associated depreciation rates for

those facilities. The Stipulation states that SPS will extend the service lives of Tolk Units 1 and 2

“from December 2027 to March 2028.” However, SPS proposed service-life extensions from

December 2028 to March 2029 in accordance with the Commission’s Final Order in Case No. 25-




                                                 1
 00066-UT. 1 Accordingly, paragraph 1.2(i) of the Stipulation should state as follows:

                 The Signatories agree to the following service-life extensions…

                 (i)      Extend the service lives of Tolk Units 1 and 2 from December 2028
                          to March 2029.

        This correction aligns the proposed service life extensions for Tolk Units 1 and 2

set forth in the Stipulation with the service life extension included in SPS’s case-in-chief.

The exhibits to the Stipulation, including the depreciation rates provided in Exhibit C,

correctly utilized the March 2029 extension date. Thus, it is only necessary to correct the

dates in the Stipulation.

        The Signatories have approved this notice, and SPS submits it on their behalf.

                                                   Respectfully submitted,

